        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Only stay in the hand with a face-up 3 if you have a strong drawing hand or made hand. The pot odds must justify the massive investment required.',
          intermediate: "Watch opponents' reactions to face-up 3s. Some players will always match, creating enormous pots that justify drawing to weaker hands.",
          advanced: 'Bluff with a face-up 3 by matching the pot with a weak hand, representing strength. This is extremely expensive but can win massive pots against cautious opponents.',
          tips: [
            'Track which 3s have been dealt face-up; the remaining 3s become less dangerous',
            "In a 6-player game, be aware that multiple face-up 3s can create pots larger than some players' stacks",
            'Consider folding marginal hands before receiving upcards to avoid the 3-penalty entirely',
          ],
